cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A floor under Newton's inequality: a sharp constant for the centred-square spectrum, and Sibuya's 1988 conjecture"
message: "If you use these results or the certificates, please cite this record."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Andrei
    family-names: Pluzhnik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5660-2603"
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked proofs of two quantitative strengthenings of Newton's inequality for the
  normalised coefficients of real-rooted polynomials: a sharp floor 4/5 for the centred-square
  spectrum, and large parts of Sibuya's 1988 conjecture for the unsigned Stirling numbers of the
  first kind. Every computation is exact rational or certified interval arithmetic, every
  certificate is an exit-0 script with a logged run, and each was validated by an independent
  re-implementation.
keywords:
  - Newton's inequalities
  - log-concavity
  - Stirling numbers of the first kind
  - Sibuya's conjecture
  - certified computation
license: MIT
